schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Priya Parker on structure and hosting spirit in gatherings
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    "Gatherings crackle and flourish when real thought goes into them, when
    (often invisible) structure is baked into them, and when a host has the
    curiosity, willingness, and generosity of spirit to try."
  evidence: >-
    Direct quotation attributed to Priya Parker, "The Art of Gathering: How
    We Meet and Why It Matters" (Riverhead Books, 2018), as cited in the
    article's References.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/gatherings-pattern.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used in the article as the founding rationale for treating gatherings as
    an intentional design challenge rather than a default "find a venue, post
    an invite" script.
  uncertainty: >-
    Quote reproduced as given in the article; page/edition location within
    the book was not independently verified for this ingestion.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/gatherings-pattern.md
    transformation: quoted
    authorship: ai-assisted
